<title>USA: Virgin Atlantic Airways adds a New York service.</title>
<headline>Virgin Atlantic Airways adds a New York service.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn. 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virgin Atlantic Airways said on Wednesday that it would run two additional flights between New York's JFK Airport and London's Heathrow Airport on July 11 in response to recent strike action against British Airways Plc.</p>
<p>The flights, one from London to New York, and the other in the opposite direction, represent a once-off service, a spokesman for Virgin told Reuters.</p>
<p>Virgin currently operates four daily nonstop flights to London from the New York area.</p>
